\section{Couplings and Effective 4D Lagrangian}

In this section we derive the effective four-dimensional Lagrangian obtained from
the STME-RS-A framework. The anharmonic bulk potential modifies the KK
wavefunctions and therefore the couplings of KK modes to Standard Model (SM)
fields. We present the full KK reduction of the action, compute gauge and fermion
couplings, and derive decay widths and branching fractions relevant for collider
phenomenology.

\subsection{KK Reduction of the Action}

We begin with the five-dimensional action
\begin{equation}
S = \int d^4x \int_0^L dy \sqrt{-g}
\left[
-\frac{1}{2}g^{MN}\partial_M\Phi\partial_N\Phi
- V(\Phi)
+ \mathcal{L}_{\text{SM}}(x,y)
\right].
\end{equation}

Expanding the scalar field in KK modes,
\begin{equation}
\Phi(x,y) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \phi_n(x) f_n(y),
\end{equation}
and integrating over the extra dimension yields the effective 4D Lagrangian
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}_{\text{eff}} =
\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}
\left[
-\frac{1}{2}\partial_\mu\phi_n\partial^\mu\phi_n
-\frac{1}{2}m_n^2\phi_n^2
\right]
+ \mathcal{L}_{\text{int}}.
\end{equation}

The interaction terms depend on the overlap integrals of KK wavefunctions with
SM fields localized on the IR brane.

