\subsection{Gauge Couplings}

Gauge fields propagate in the bulk with zero-mode profiles flat in $y$. The KK
modes couple to gauge fields via
\begin{equation}
g_n = g_5 \int_0^L dy\, e^{-ky} f_n(y),
\end{equation}
where $g_5$ is the five-dimensional gauge coupling.

Anharmonicity increases IR localization of $f_n(y)$, enhancing $g_n$.

\begin{figure}[h!]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.75\textwidth]{fig_gauge_couplings.pdf}
\caption{Gauge couplings $g_n$ for BP1--BP4. Anharmonicity increases IR
localization and enhances couplings for higher KK modes.}
\label{fig:gauge_couplings}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Fermion Localization}

Fermions propagate in the bulk with localization determined by their bulk mass
parameter $c$:
\begin{equation}
\psi(x,y) = e^{(2-c)ky}\psi(x).
\end{equation}

The coupling of KK modes to fermions is
\begin{equation}
g_{n,f} = g_5 \int_0^L dy\, e^{-3ky} f_n(y) e^{(2-c)ky}.
\end{equation}

For IR-localized fermions ($c<1/2$), the coupling is enhanced.

